  "Preregistered hypotheses: all confirmed in the tested finite classes. Each claim is a hypothesis of PLAN.md section 3 tested in finite toy classes; this is not a verdict on the framework's resolution of the paradox.",
  "Headline: bijectivity does not imply recovery from the accessible records (counterexamples), and is not necessary for it; with bijectivity, complete endpoint access is sufficient for exact recovery, and an inaccessible endpoint set K bounds the loss by P_succ >= 1/|K|.",
